n us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been marked unhealthy. I rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 49847, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0175ft3z2i218DyTY3VGUWQ9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49847, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0175ft3z2i218DyTY3VGUWQ9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54180, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been marked unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy, so I rolled back to it. All three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n- **After:** The service reports healthy, with about a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is titled \"checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0\". It records what failed, the rollback and how the service looks now. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before redeploying that version.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016qLGarY7jDEZMbGhd3sk59", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018swxcr8tcQSzRXwkPJa5ao", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Svp1rpHSfVXVC429nLR4BJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TjzpxZSX8aP2r8JddR987L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LuGhddyyQgt2pgW9g9tUFe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0175ft3z2i218DyTY3VGUWQ9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api started failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy, running in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been marked unhealthy. I rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been marked unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy, so I rolled back to it. All three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n- **After:** The service reports healthy, with about a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is titled \"checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0\". It records what failed, the rollback and how the service looks now. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before redeploying that version.", "type": "text"}]}]}